  "interpretation": [
    "This is a separate screening sensitivity using the existing constant-power proxy assumptions.",
    "The screen conditions jointly on all candidate cases: six cells per common-cohort block and four per extension block. It is not each family's separate conditional distribution.",
    "Within each owner, the admitted finite set approximates a constrained parameter law; it is not a fitted dependence model or parameter-estimation uncertainty.",
    "The finite bank reuses the saved proposal indices; its size does not establish convergence to a continuous constrained sampling law.",
    "Retain one test vehicle per source owner and choose an admitted index uniformly within that owner, using the same index across compared cases. Never sample owners by flattening the retained row pool.",
    "The distribution-change table averages within owners first, then gives each source owner equal weight. After-screen means are blank if any owner in that cohort has no admitted draw.",
    "An owner with no admitted index stays in the audit and blocks a pilot for the full cohort; it is not silently dropped or imputed.",
    "Admitted values and battery flags are copied exactly; excluded blocks remain in the audit and original source package.",
    "This necessary mean-time screen does not establish actual scheduling feasibility, completed-frequency agreement, battery compatibility or an observed electrical boundary.",
    "The 168-hour allowance is optimistic: driving, dwell availability, acceptance limits, taper and station constraints require further modelling.",
    "The selected source cohorts and equal-owner test weights do not estimate national fleet composition."
